XPolicyLab ACT changes used by the cross-embodiment transfer study.

These live inside the XPolicyLab submodule, which tracks upstream
XPolicyLab/XPolicyLab. Committing them there would record a submodule SHA
that exists on no remote and break every clone, so they are carried here as
a patch against the pinned submodule commit instead.

Base:   XPolicyLab c37109c (v1.0.0~7), the SHA recorded in this repo.
Apply:  git -C XPolicyLab apply ../patches/xpolicylab-act-study.patch
Verify: git -C XPolicyLab apply --check ../patches/xpolicylab-act-study.patch

What it changes:
  imitate_episodes.py, detr/main.py
      --resume_ckpt and --start_epoch. A resume MUST pass --start_epoch: the
      loop is range(start_epoch, num_epochs) and checkpoints are named
      policy_epoch_{epoch+1}, so resuming without it restarts at 0 and
      overwrites lower-epoch checkpoints with over-trained weights.
      detr/main.py re-parses sys.argv, so each new flag is mirrored there.
  utils.py
      A per-dataset episode spec may be an explicit index LIST, not only a
      count; the scene-controlled T=32 arms need this. Dataloader workers
      and prefetch are configurable via ACT_NUM_WORKERS / ACT_PREFETCH.
  train.sh
      Threads RESUME_CKPT and START_EPOCH through to imitate_episodes.py.
  setup_eval_policy_server.sh
      Accepts a uv/venv path in place of a conda env name; computes the
      action width for the chosen action_type (joint or ee); finds
      checkpoints nested one level deep under checkpoints/<task>/.
  run_sim_env_client.sh
      Accepts a uv/venv path in place of a conda env name.
  get_action_dim.sh, process_data.py
      action_type argument: end-effector (ee) packing and widths alongside
      joint. Defaults to joint so existing callers are unchanged.
  utils/robot/_robot_info.json
      Registers ur5 and the grid-arm names (cotrain4, gridk*, scene40k*,
      scene80k4). Nothing is removed; the file is also reordered.

